C=45^°

d_{real}=n,d_{apparent}



d_{real}=frac43×2.7=3.6 m


The real depth is greater than the apparent depth. Option A incorrectly divides the apparent depth by the refractive index.

n=frac1{sin C}
=frac1{sin30^°}
=frac1{0.5}=2


Option A gives sin C instead of its reciprocal.

u=-10 cm,quad f=+15 cm



frac1v-frac1{-10}=frac1{15}



frac1v=frac1{15}-frac1{10}=-frac1{30}


Hence v=-30 cm and m=v/u=+3. The image is virtual, erect and magnified.
